@inherits HowToFlashFirmwarePageBase

@page "/FlashFirmware"

<br />
<MudImage Src="./Projects/Images/esp32.svg" Width="600" Class="rounded-lg"> </MudImage>
<br />
<br />
<MudText>1. Install <MudLink OnClick="@(() => OpenBrowserTab("https://code.visualstudio.com/"))">Visual Studio Code (VS Code)</MudLink></MudText>
<br />
<MudText>2. Install <MudLink OnClick="@(() => OpenBrowserTab("https://platformio.org/"))">Platform IO</MudLink></MudText>
<br />
<MudText>3. Optional: Install WOKWI for VS Code if you want to simulate an ESP32 microcontroller and do not have a real one yet. <MudLink Href="https://docs.wokwi.com/vscode/getting-started">WOKWI</MudLink></MudText>
<br />
<MudText>4. Open the solution in Visual Studio Code with PlatformIO</MudText>
<br />
<MudImage Src="./Projects/Images/platformioopenproject.png" Width="600" Class="rounded-lg"> </MudImage>
<br />
<br />
<MudText>Navigate to the folder that contains platformio.ini and click the button 'Open "Microcontroller"'.</MudText>
<br />
<MudImage Src="./Projects/Images/platformioopenproject2.png" Width="600" Class="rounded-lg"></MudImage>
<br />
<br />
<MudText>5. Open defines.cpp</MudText>
<br />
<MudImage Src="./Projects/Images/openmaincpp.png" Width="900" Class="rounded-lg"></MudImage>
<MudText>Uncomment the #define lines for all devices you want to connect to your microcontroller.</MudText>
<br />
<MudText>6. Open ConnectionSettings.hpp and enter your WiFi settings.</MudText>
<br />
<MudText>7. Connect the microcontroller via USB, or skip this step if you use WOKWI.</MudText>
<br />
<MudText>8. Compile and upload the firmware to the microcontroller.</MudText>
<br />
<MudImage Src="./Projects/Images/upload.png" Width="600" Class="rounded-lg"> </MudImage>
<br />
<br />
<MudText>9. Optional: To <b>simulate the microcontroller</b>, press F1 in VS Code and choose Wokwi: Start Simulator.</MudText>
<MudImage Src="./Projects/Images/startsimulator.png" Width="900" Class="rounded-lg"> </MudImage>
<MudText>Edit <MudLink OnClick="@(() => OpenBrowserTab("https://docs.wokwi.com/diagram-format/"))" >diagram.json</MudLink>. This file defines the simulated components, their properties, and how they are connected.</MudText>
